   "daf": "28b",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ פְּתִילַת הַבֶּגֶד שֶׁקִּיפְּלָהּ וְלֹא הִבְהֲבָהּ, רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר אוֹמֵר: טְמֵאָה הִיא, וְאֵין מַדְלִיקִין בָּהּ. רַבִּי עֲקִיבָא אוֹמֵר טְהוֹרָה הִיא, וּמַדְלִיקִין בָּהּ.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» «The wick of a garment,» i.e., cloth made into a wick for a lamp, «that one folded it» into a size and shape suitable for a wick, «but did not» yet «singe it» slightly in order to facilitate its lighting, «Rabbi Eliezer says:» This wick is «ritually impure.» With regard to the laws of ritual impurity, it can, like other garments, still become ritually impure «and one may not light with it» on Shabbat. «Rabbi Akiva says: It is ritually pure and one may» even «light with it» on Shabbat."
  }
 ],
